  "uprn": "100023407008",
  "decision_date": "23/12/2004",
  "description": "Demolition of existing bulding and the erection of 19 x apartments (5 x three bed, 13 x two bed and 1 x one bed) associated landscaping and the creation of 28 car parking spaces, provision of a river walking and restoration of the historic crane",
  "site_name": "Riverside Mill House",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "23/12/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW7 6XB",
  "street_name": "Church Street",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "22/12/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposal seeks to redevelop a brownfield site, which is supported by council, London and National guidance, and provide homes that would help the council meet its housing targets. A case has been made for the loss of employment uses on the site, and the principle of residential development and affordable housing is considered to be appropriate. The development serves to enhance the character and appearance of the Conservation Area and improves access to the riverside.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority (before the building(s) is/are occupied/used).",
    "Condition : 4 - 3.\tNo development shall take place above existing ground level until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted scheme have been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 5 - 4.\tNo development shall take place above existing ground level until detailed drawings of the proposed balconies and railings have been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 6 - 5.\tNo demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am and 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 8:30 and 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Bank Holidays.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - 6.\tBefore commencement of the development details shall be submitted to and approved by the LPA to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\nMeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\nMeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved shall be fully implement on commencement of development.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place above existing ground level until details of cycle parking for the residents been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA. The spaces shown on any of the approved drawings shall be available for use before first occupation of the buildings and permanently maintained and retained thereafter",
    "Condition : 9 - 8.\tBefore the development is commenced a scheme to deal with contamination on the site and pollution of the water environment shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA and such scheme shall be implemented strictly in accordance with the terms of any approval and completed in respect of each building before it is first occupied.",
    "Condition : 10 - 9.\tThe contamination scheme shall include an investigation and assessment to identify the extent of contamination and to determine its potential for the pollution of the water environment.  The scheme shall also include measures to be taken to avoid risk to the public, buildings, and environment to prevent pollution of groundwater and surface water and provisions for monitoring contamination when the site is developed.  The scheme for dealing with the contamination shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 11 - 10.\tNo development shall take place until the applicant has secured the implementation of a programme of archaeological work in accordance with a written scheme of investigation (including the timetable for the investigation) which has been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA.",
    "Condition : 12 - 11.\tNo development shall take place until details of the design of the construction of the surface water drainage system has been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA including a timetable for implementation and such scheme shall be implemented in accordance with the terms of any approval.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 13 - 12.\tNo development shall take place above existing ground level until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected including all internal boundary treatments and railings.  All boundary treatments shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or in accordance with a timetable to be agreed in writing with the LPA.  The boundary treatments shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 14 - 13.\tNo development shall take place above existing ground level until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 15 - The hard landscape details shall include; proposed finished levels; means of enclosure; vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas; hard surfacing materials; street furniture including seats, cycle racks, safety railings, refuse units; and lighting.",
    "Condition : 16 - 15.\tThe soft landscape details shall include: planting plans including full details of all proposed tree planting; written specifications including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment; schedules of plants noting species which should incorporate appropriate native species alongside the watercourses; plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate; implementation programme including proposed times of planting.  All  trees planted within 16m of the flood defences inner walls shall have anti-root film or root containment systems.",
    "Condition : 17 - 16.\tAll hard and soft landscaping shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.  The works shall be carried out prior to the occupation of any part of the development or in accordance with the programme agreed with the LPA in writing.",
    "Condition : 18 - 17.\tNo development above existing ground level shall take place until a landscape management plan, including long term design objectives, management responsibilities, arrangements for implementation and maintenance schedules for all hard and soft landscape areas for a minimum of 5 years has been submitted to and approved by the LPA.  The landscape management and maintenance plan shall be carried out in accordance with the approved schedule.",
    "Condition : 19 - The development hereby permitted shall not begin until details of the arrangements for storing of refuse or waste have been submitted to and approved by the LPA.  The arrangements for storing of refuse or waste shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with an approval given and shall be completed before any part of the development hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 20 - 19.\tNo additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in any wall of the development hereby approved without the prior written consent of the LPA.",
    "Condition : 21 - Development shall not commence until a survey of existing ground levels have been submitted.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 22 - The ground levels shall not be raised or otherwise altered from those shown on the plan approved by the l.p.a. pursuant to the above condition without the prior written approval of the l.p.a.",
    "Condition : 23 - No development approved by this planning permission shall be commenced until an assessment of the life of the flood defences and river wall, with an accompanying plan to ensure the life of the flood defences is commensurate with the life of the development, is submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. These measures shall not create adverse environmental or structural impacts, encroachment into the river channel, or entailing works that are disproportionate to the scale of the development. The scheme shall be constructed and completed in accordance with the approved plans.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 24 - No development shall take place above existing ground level until details of a scheme to demonstrate that the flats hereby approved are built to 'lifetime homes' standard, such scheme shall be implemented prior to occupation of any of the units."
